<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       ORBIT LAYER SIZE

       Odyssey's orbit layer is generated as an icosphere with HALF the
       subdivision depth of the planet surface:

           Core   Surface : radius 100, subdivisions 10
           Odyssey Orbit  : radius 130, subdivisions 5

       Tile count is EXACTLY 12 + 10 * (3^subdivisions - 1). It scales with
       ~3^subdivisions, not 4^. PlanetLayer.Subdivide emits one new vertex
       per triangle and one triangle per (vertex, adjacent-triangle) pair,
       so triangles triple each pass and the surviving degree-5/6 vertices
       are the tiles. Verified against 1.6.4871 rev590.

           subdivisions 5 :  2,432 tiles
           subdivisions 6 :  7,292 tiles
           subdivisions 7 : 21,872 tiles

       Orbit therefore has orders of magnitude fewer tiles than the surface.
       Since PlanetLayerDef.Orbit sets settlementsPer100kTiles to 1000~1000
       (one settlement per ~100 tiles), a small tile count also means very
       few orbital settlements, asteroids and points of interest: roughly
       9 at subdivisions 5, roughly 27 at 6.

       Raising subdivisions by 1 multiplies tile count by roughly 3, and
       scales settlements/sites/travel distance with it.

       COST: worldgen time and orbit mesh vertex count grow with the same
       factor. 5 to 6 is the conservative step. 6 to 7 is another ~3x, NOT
       the 16x an earlier draft of this comment claimed, which came from the
       wrong scaling law. Try it only after confirming 6 generates in
       acceptable time.

       MULTIPLAYER: this is a def, so both clients get an identical value
       as long as they run the same mod version.

       WORLDGEN-ONLY. See docs/TRAPS.md T-45. PlanetLayer.ExposeData scribes
       subdivisions/radius/viewAngle/viewCenter, and InitializeLayer()
       rebuilds the icosphere from the SCRIBED values, not from the def.
       Editing this patch after a world exists is a silent no-op; it must be
       right before world creation, alongside the faction roster (T-07).

       NOTE the leading slash on the xpath below. tools/defdb.py currently
       evaluates a leading-"Defs/" xpath relative to the Defs element and
       matches nothing while still reporting success (issue #102), so the
       absolute "/Defs/..." form here is the one that verifies correctly.

       NOTE ALSO: no double hyphen anywhere in this comment. Two hyphens in
       a row terminate an XML comment early and RimWorld drops the whole
       file with no error. That is T-01, and this comment tripped it once.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/PlanetLayerSettingsDef[defName="Orbit"]/settings/subdivisions</xpath>
    <value>
      <subdivisions>6</subdivisions>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
